						<a href="/forum/t-13953085/seeking-greenlight-host-of-the-eldritch-abomination">[Seeking Greenlight] Host of the Eldritch Abomination.</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4853610">
									

<p>Heyo followup! :)</p>
<p><strong>SAND</strong></p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>The concept:</strong></p>
<blockquote>
<p>Elevator Pitch: Janual Grey is a mixed-race of a human and a Lovecraftian-horror, he is a space-time, reality-altering Lovecraftian horror who uncontrollably goes on a frenzy to satisfy his hunger when not consuming any nutritious food.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is much more concise than the initial EP. My only real concern here is the vagueness of the effects; &quot;space-time altering&quot; and &quot;reality altering&quot; are fairly broad terms. What specifically can the skip do?</p>
<p>For this to work, you will need a strong narrative behind it, as the concept on its own won't be enough to carry the article, the frequency this sort of premise is seen, also contributes heavily to this needing a strong narrative. -The concept could appear cliched or hard to get invested in otherwise.</p>
<p>I would recommend you work on exploring the skip itself more in the narrative, and work on expanding on the current points you have in the EP. Other than that however, I don't much of a problem with this initially.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>He discovers his powers shortly after the seal implanted by his father has worn off while he's camping at Acadia-National-Park. Due to having a monstrous-form and nature, he didn't want to hurt the innocents, so he ran away from society. During his times in the woods, Janual started to use his powers to transport bad peoples, usually from high-security prisons or those who have faced death penalties, to the forest and consumes them to restrain the hostile nature he embodies.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>IMO this doesn't seem necessary to the pitch, as this is fairly specific info that looks closer to what you would see (at least in part) in the narrative summary. That said though, one of my biggest issues is the cannibalism. Considering the skip is compassionate, I have trouble believing that it could justify eating any humans. I'm also unsure on how the skip knows exactly which prisoners are in what sentence. Overall, eating humans (from what I've gathered) is optional for the skip, considering if it really needed to, it could eat an animal or live off wild grown food.</p>
<p>If you want to depict the skip eating other humans; you would need to have a strong reason behind it, along with showing how the skip reacts to/ feels about doing it. If they have morals then doing such a thing would affect them heavily.- as quick note with this, do make sure to handle the topic carefully. Try not to just allow the skip to go and eat people point blank.</p>
<p><strong>The narrative:</strong></p>
<blockquote>
<p>Since being held in Foundation custody after reports of prisoners went missing and their corpses being found in the woods. At the same time, they also learned that he has a relationship with SCP-105 as being her school friend and his hungry nature that happened every 24 hours after an incident where he forgot to eat.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I would still recommend you phase SCP-105 out, it doesn't really contribute anything and considering its a series one skip, may be seen as a quick way to gain attention.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The shocking truth was:</p>
<p>His father is an eldritch abomination named &quot;Darkness&quot; worshiped by a cult named &quot;Allies-of-&quot;Darkness&quot; as they have succeeded in summoning it into their reality. Janual's father disguised as a human and seduced his mother into having a baby while visiting the church. When Janual was born, his father secretly implanted a seal to prevent him from exposing his powers. It wants Janual to become the next &quot;Darkness&quot;. Janual explained this after the cult was given an order by his father to free him after they've received its &quot;universal-message&quot; through telepathic communications, which also bestowing them reality-bending powers. However, they were killed shortly after finishing the explanation when not paying attention to the MTF arriving.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Overall, this is still closer to an explanation than anything. I'm still not given a clear story arc, or any major events, or any clear idea on how the concept and narrative will be executed in the draft. While there is a story here, it's too vague to really grasp or understand, as there is not lead up or explanation as to how the Foundation knows about certain things (ie. the cult).</p>
<p>My previous concerns with the narrative still hold up. I would highly recommend you start developing a narrative straight away, the context you currently have in place of the narrative can be replaced or taken out if they don't contribute to the overall arc.</p>
<p><strong>Red or green?</strong><br />
Due to my afore mentioned concerns, no-greenlight.</p>
<p>-this needs a narrative more than anything, without one, I wouldn't be comfortable giving a greenlight.</p>
<p>If you would like me review this (or any concept) further, then please feel free to send me a PM or ask via IRC. Response times generally range from 2-12 hours over PMs. If your looking for additional critiques in general, then I would highly recommend contacting the butterfly squad :)</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Cheers,</p>
<p>-RED</p>

